FQN: Example: Table Shapes Are Invisible to shapes() but Reachable via table_count/table_at
Kind: verified_example
Provenance: authored
Verification: passed
Authored example: written for foss-mcp against the pinned library, not taken from the upstream README; published only after the ingestion verifier compiled or ran it against that commit.
Verification-Level: ran-exit0
Verified-With: g++ (Debian 14.2.0-19) 14.2.0

Adds a table to a slide's shape collection and shows the real, documented hazard of this pilot's shapes() model directly, that a table never grows shapes().size() the way an AutoShape or Connector does, and the only correct way to reach it back is the separate table_count()/table_at() pair; also writes and reads back real cell text through Cell.text_frame().

Example:
// Authored example: add a table and show it never grows shapes() but is reachable via table_count/table_at.
#include <cassert>
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>

#include <Aspose/Slides/Foss/cell.h>
#include <Aspose/Slides/Foss/presentation.h>
#include <Aspose/Slides/Foss/shape_collection.h>
#include <Aspose/Slides/Foss/slide.h>
#include <Aspose/Slides/Foss/table.h>
#include <Aspose/Slides/Foss/text_frame.h>

using namespace Aspose::Slides::Foss;

int main() {
    Presentation pres;
    auto& shapes = pres.slides()[0].shapes();

    const std::vector<double> column_widths{120.0, 120.0};
    const std::vector<double> row_heights{30.0, 30.0};
    auto& table = shapes.add_table(20, 20, column_widths, row_heights);
    table.cell(0, 0).text_frame()->set_text("Name");
    table.cell(0, 1).text_frame()->set_text("Score");
    table.cell(1, 0).text_frame()->set_text("Ada");
    table.cell(1, 1).text_frame()->set_text("98");

    std::cout << "shapes().size(): " << shapes.size() << '\n';
    std::cout << "table_count(): " << shapes.table_count() << '\n';
    std::cout << "cell(1,1): " << table.cell(1, 1).text_frame()->text() << '\n';

    assert(shapes.size() == 0);
    assert(shapes.table_count() == 1);
    assert(&shapes.table_at(0) == &table);
    assert(table.cell(1, 1).text_frame()->text() == "98");
    return 0;
}
